          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Human_caudal_spinal_cord_anterior_view_description" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
      <floats-group id="article-38327.s14">
        <fig id="article-38327.image.f5" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Cauda Equina Syndrome. This magnetic resonance image shows&#x000a0;a large central disc herniation and severe spinal stenosis at the L5-S1 level that causes&#x000a0;displacement of the cauda equina nerve roots. This condition requires&#x000a0;urgent medical attention. Contributed by Sunil Munakomi, MD</p>
          </caption>
